ok
uses of &lt;noscript&gt;: ads (document.write+&lt;noscript&gt;), tracking (script + &lt;noscript&gt;&lt;img&gt;), inclusion of flash (plugin detection with script + &lt;noscript&gt;&lt;object&gt;)
from analysing the first 10 pages in http://canvex.lazyilluminati.com/misc/stats/2/analyse.cgi/tag/noscript
the first doesn't work at all in xml. the second neither, since &lt;img&gt;s are always loaded (except in opera). the third might work
