:P
It's not a port of anything
The code is actually all mine
except the boot rom, because, you know, it's the actual boot rom used internally on the nintendo GameBoy Color.
I converted the bin dump by costis to a javascript friendly hex array for that. :P
The boot rom that was supposed to be un-dumpable
and dumped in fall '09
Way later than the GBA dump, because the boot rom hid itself from the memory map once the lockout register was tripped.
the GBA BIOS ROM just needed a subroutine to be exploited to be dumped, since it was still mapped, but blocked off from reading
so the trick there was for the GBA BIOS ROM to dump itself
by using a MIDI subroutine to read bytes of the boot rom memory, that nintendo forgot to block the BIOS from reading itself for.
:P
FTFY: making read-protected BIOS read itself out to homebrew ROMs. :P
but the GBC boot ROM needed manual hackery
to fuck up the CPU itself to not lock the boot ROM memory from the memory itself
